Subject: [PATCH 3/3] sglang: get the bpreshuffle FP8 scale layout from the quant
 kernel instead of a transposing copy

Base:        sglang @ 29481685462732237d80d86076d6563e1f658102 (/sgl-workspace/sglang)
Pristine:    patches/base/sglang-29481685-fp8_utils.py, obtained with
               git show HEAD:python/sglang/srt/layers/quantization/fp8_utils.py
             and verified byte-identical (cmp) to the untouched working tree before
             any edit. The sglang checkout carries unrelated local modifications;
             this file was clean at HEAD.
Applies on:  top of patches 0001 and 0002 (independent of both -- it touches sglang,
             they touch aiter -- but it was only ever measured with them applied).

WHAT
    On gfx95 with B-preshuffle, ``aiter_w8a8_block_fp8_linear`` quantised the
    activation to a row-major [M, G] scale and then reshaped it into the
    column-major arrangement the GEMM consumes with

        scale.t().contiguous().t()

    which is a real transposing copy kernel, launched once per FP8 GEMM.
    ``per_group_quant_hip`` can emit those bytes directly via its
    ``transpose_scale`` argument (``shuffle_scale`` inside the kernel), leaving
    only a stride reinterpretation -- no launch, no traffic.

    A comment in aiter's own
    ``aiter/dist/device_communicators/communicator_cuda.py:541`` claims the quant
    kernel "cannot produce that stride directly ... a different physical
    arrangement". That is not true for this shape family, and the claim is what
    kept the copy in place. Disproved directly: for (64, 5120) and (64, 17408),
    ``transpose_scale=True`` returns a quantised tensor ``torch.equal`` to the
    ``transpose_scale=False`` one, and ``torch.as_strided(s, s.shape, (1, M))``
    is ``torch.equal`` to ``s.t().contiguous().t()``, with matching raw storage
    bytes. The GEMM therefore sees identical values behind identical strides.

MEASUREMENT (frozen configuration: ISL 8192 / OSL 1024 / concurrency 64 /
192 prompts / 8 warmups / random ratio 1.0 / ignore_eos / seed 0 / TP=1)

    Interleaved across-restart A/B, A B A B, four fresh server instances, three
    runs each, compared position-matched (run i of A against run i of B).
    Required by measurement.md Rule 6b + 3b: this machine's SCLK free-runs
